<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Dec '96 overdue loan ratio at 3.78 pct.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Dec '96 overdue loan ratio at 3.78 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan domestic banks' overdue loans in end-December 1996 accounted for 3.78 percent of their total loans, down from end-September's 3.89 percent but up from end-June's 3.47 percent, the central bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The total value of bank loans in end-December was T$9.496 trillion, the central bank said in a statement. It did not give a monetary total for overdue loans.</p>
<p>The bank usually announces the ratio on a quarterly basis.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
